bridge(14,7,22,23,'mediation_test','supports','The anti-CD3-associated FOXP3 protein response depends partly on endogenous IL2 activity in the PBMC culture, supported by neutralization and IL2 competition.','IL2 is the perturbed intermediate; FOXP3 intracellular protein is the common downstream endpoint. Upstream source-cell IL2 secretion is not identified.','Anti-CD3 and blockade startt=0; FOXP3 measured24h. Schedule supports intervention ordering, not a measured secretion→STAT5→FOXP3 trajectory.','Direct FOXP3 flow under CD3 activation, IL2 antibody blockade and exogenous IL2 competition.','Same PBMC protocol; Fig1 and Fig3 exact donor overlap unavailable. Four blocking experiments; no purified-cell transfer.','Neither antibody fully inhibitory alone; mixed-cell indirect effects possible. No STAT5 assay or stable Treg-function claim.')
bridge(15,7,23,24,'mediation_test','supports','Neutralization/CD25 blockade and IL2 competition strengthen the narrow IL2/CD25 dependence of FOXP3 induction; high combined blockade resists10nM IL2 rescue.','Same IL2 protein/receptor interaction perturbed by antibodies and competitive supplementation; no claim of downstream STAT5 mediation.','Blockade and ligand added atactivation; FOXP3 assay24h.','Intracellular FOXP3 with dose-dependent antibody/ligand conditions.','Same source PBMC assay; exact donor pairing across panels unavailable,4 experiments reported.','Competitive rescue is concentration dependent. High combined blocker failure is retained; a complete negative-feedback loop is not established.')
bridge(16,7,22,25,'context_contrast','opposes','FOXP3 induction in activated PBMCs does not by itself establish suppression of neighboring FOXP3-negative-cell IL2 responses.','FOXP3 protein frequency versus intracellular IL2 in a different gate; no translation or serial regulatory inference.','Initial24h activation followed by6h restimulation in separate experiment.','Both intracellular flow, not purified Treg suppression or secretion assays.','Same source PBMC culture; baseline and restimulation donors overlap unavailable.','Does not oppose all Treg suppressive activity; culture ratios, timing and activated non-Treg FOXP3 expression matter.')
bridge(17,8,21,20,'mediation_test','inconclusive','RBPJ/HDAC3 repression and RBPJ-dependent suppression are promising follow-up hypotheses, blocked until complete primary wet-lab Methods and Results are inspected.','FOXP3 expression and suppressive function remain distinct; even HDAC3-dependent FOXP3 repression would not demonstrate FOXP3 mediation of suppression.','Full intervention and endpoint timing unavailable.','Public figure captions and analytical supplement only; main wet-lab Methods/Results inaccessible.','Same paper; Fig4n=4,Fig3jn=3; donor overlap unavailable.','Source correction adds competing-interest disclosure. No claims from mouse-host GvHD transported into human in vivo.',status='blocked_missing_evidence',checks={'entity_continuity':'not_demonstrated','context_compatibility':'not_demonstrated','temporal_compatibility':'not_demonstrated','measurement_link':'not_demonstrated','experimental_linkage':'not_demonstrated','mediation_test':'not_demonstrated'})
